# Wazuh Manager Setup

## Overview
This document provides instructions on setting up a **Wazuh Manager** on a **Google Cloud Virtual Machine (VM)** with the specified configurations.

## Virtual Machine Specifications
- **RAM**: 8GB+
- **HDD**: 50GB+
- **OS**: Ubuntu 22.04 LTS

## Installation Steps
### 1. Set Up the Virtual Machine
1. Log in to your **Google Cloud Console**.
2. Navigate to **Compute Engine > VM Instances**.
3. Click **Create Instance**.
4. Configure the instance:
   - **Machine Type**: At least 8GB RAM
   - **Boot Disk**: Ubuntu 22.04 LTS with at least 50GB storage
5. Allow HTTP and HTTPS traffic if needed.
6. Click **Create** and wait for the VM to be provisioned.

### 2. Install Wazuh Manager
Run the following command on your VM:
```sh
curl -sO https://packages.wazuh.com/4.7/wazuh-install.sh && sudo bash ./wazuh-install.sh -a
```

### 3. Retrieve Default Credentials
After installation, take note of the default credentials displayed at the end of the setup.
If you missed it, retrieve them from the **wazuh-install-files.tar** archive:
```sh
tar -xvf wazuh-install-files.tar
```

### 4. Verify Wazuh Installation
Run the following command to check the Wazuh service status:
```sh
sudo systemctl status wazuh-manager
```
If Wazuh is running successfully, you should see an active status.

